    dict_struct_key_identity_keyed_copied_key_misses_2026-09-13, 0, "2026-11-27 p3sweep-20261127: measured on fresh HEAD seed. Tree-walk interpreter: struct Point keys FIXED (canonical sorted-field Value::Object arm, value_impl.rs:225-233) - copied/rebound lookups hit, twins one bucket; class Point keys LIVE (to_key_string had no ClassInstance arm -> derived-Debug catch-all value_impl.rs:291 with per-instance HashMap field order -> equal twins get different key strings while == is structural). Patch A implemented in src/compiler_rust/compiler/src/value_impl.rs:234-249 (ClassInstance arm producing canonical sorted-field form); cargo check PASS, not built per lane constraint - needs seed rebuild to take effect. Native/JIT lane LIVE for BOTH struct and class keys: raw rt_alloc blocks carry no type metadata (mir expr_dispatch.spl:2395-2402) so C runtime (runtime_native.c:13754 pointer hash, :5850 identity eq) and Rust twin (equality.rs:213 fnv of raw bits, :297 false) fall back to identity; a sound structural hash is impossible without layout registration - needs the language-level decision this doc calls for. Adjacent hazard observed: d[missing_struct_key] index syntax returns raw flat-nil sentinel decoded as 3 instead of nil on the native lane. Regression pin test/01_unit/lib/common/dict_struct_key_structural_identity_spec.spl 6/6 PASS on interpreter lane. close_evidence reproducer=test/01_unit/lib/common/dict_struct_key_structural_identity_spec.spl prevention=test/01_unit/lib/common/dict_native_shape_differential_spec.spl"

